  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="need-nooks"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">02 / Start with the job</p><h2>Does a team of five or ten<br>actually need Nooks?</h2><p>Headcount alone is a weak reason to buy. Work out where callers lose useful time and what the existing setup already handles.</p></div>
    <div class="nk-decisions"><div><p class="lp-kicker">Keep what works</p><h3>Calls and follow-up already run well.</h3><p>Your reps can reach the right record, make the call and see the next action. A new subscription needs to improve something specific. Recording and AI notes alone offer little value when you already have them.</p></div><div><p class="lp-kicker">Try a smaller addition</p><h3>Reps spend too long waiting.</h3><p>A clean queue of suitable contacts produces too much ringing and too few conversations. Test power or parallel calling with the tools you have, then compare a separate dialler if the gap remains.</p></div><div><p class="lp-kicker">Consider the team platform</p><h3>Managers will use the extra tools.</h3><p>Regular calling sessions, live coaching and shared reporting have a clear owner. A larger platform can earn its cost when the team uses those features and the trial shows an improvement worth keeping.</p></div></div>
    <div class="nk-two nk-after" id="nooks-pricing"><div><h3>Nooks pricing: the missing number.</h3><p>Nooks asks buyers to request a custom quote. Its public pricing page lists capabilities without a dollar price for the package your team needs. That puts a sales conversation in front of a basic budget decision.</p><p>We would ask for an itemised offer early: paid seats, dialler, coaching, data, usage, onboarding and full term. Get that price before deciding whether an alternative costs less.</p></div><div><h3>What does Nooks actually offer?</h3><p>Nooks combines power and parallel calling, CRM sync, number reputation tools, coaching and a virtual salesfloor. A team using those together has a reason to investigate it.</p><p>Its FAQ also says most customers keep their primary data provider. Include the subscriptions you will retain when deciding what the Nooks package replaces.</p></div></div>
    <p class="lp-sources"><a href="https://www.nooks.ai/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nooks pricing, features and data-provider FAQ ↗</a></p>
    <div class="lp-note"><strong>CallTeam verdict: price the simpler options first.</strong><p>A small team should be able to check affordability before sitting through a demo. Nooks needs to show what improvement earns its additional cost. A recognisable brand and a list of AI features are weak reasons to sign.</p></div>
  </div></section>

