  <section class="lp-section" id="switching"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">05 / Protect the next conversation</p><h2>Check callbacks<br>before you switch.</h2><p>A prospect can return a call days after your dialling session. Decide where that call will land before moving numbers or cancelling a tool.</p></div>
    <div class="nk-two"><div><h3>Can you keep the phone numbers?</h3><p>Nooks' terms say numbers it provisions cannot be ported or retained after the applicable order ends. This applies specifically to Nooks-provisioned numbers. Check your order and arrange callback coverage before leaving.</p><p class="lp-sources"><a href="https://www.nooks.ai/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nooks terms, section 9: phone numbers ↗</a></p><h3>Will the history follow?</h3><p>Export the call outcomes, notes, recordings you need and outstanding follow-ups. Confirm ownership and next actions in the new system before the old access ends.</p></div><div><h3>What happens when someone answers?</h3><p>Test a human answer, voicemail, an AI screening assistant, a switchboard and a callback. For parallel calling, test two answers at once. Hear what the prospect hears and check how each outcome is recorded.</p><p>Compare similar lists and calling blocks. Track useful conversations, clean follow-up and held meetings. A bigger dial count can hide poor contact quality or rushed conversations.</p><p>Use the <a href="/resources/best-cold-calling-dialers/#trial-scorecard">free dialler trial kit</a> and our <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/">mobile vs company number guide</a> to prepare the test.</p></div></div>
